+## Instruction and assessment design
 
-## Cognia Eligibility Requirements
+Video playlists, written reflection, assignments, portfolios and capstones are documented design choices. Published video resources and repository files establish availability; they do not establish attendance, mastery or credit. Use restricted submissions and human rubric review for identifiable learner work. Public posts should contain only appropriately authorized, de-identified evidence.
 
-Before submitting an application, SydTek Scholars must demonstrate:
+## Workload and credit reconciliation
 
-1. **Operational history:** 12+ consecutive months of student enrollment
-2. **Governing board:** Functioning board of trustees with documented meetings and resolutions
-3. **Financial soundness:** Audited or reviewed financial statements
-4. **Curriculum documentation:** All courses have learning outcomes, scope & sequence, assessment rubrics
-5. **Seat time documentation:** All courses meet minimum instructional hour requirements
-6. **Student records:** FERPA-compliant recordkeeping system
-7. **Mission and vision:** Documented institutional mission aligned with Cognia standards
-8. **Faculty qualifications:** Instructors meet or exceed qualification standards for grade level
-9. **Technology infrastructure:** Reliable delivery platform with documented uptime
+The old five-hour course model (200 minutes of video plus 100 minutes of reflection) produces 150 hours for 30 courses, or about 200 hours after an assumed 50 project hours. Other files use 440 minutes per course and annual bands of 40/60/84 hours. These are incompatible planning bases, not measured attendance or an accreditor-approved equivalency.
 
----
+Adopt one reviewed workload policy with course/version, expected activity time, actual participation, assessment and applicable credit basis. Keep estimated and observed time separate. No academic credit, dual enrollment, automatic progression or transfer portability is approved by these calculations.
 
-## Educational Model Documentation
+## Evidence closeout
 
-### Instructional Delivery
-- **Primary:** YouTube-based structured playlists (video-first instruction)
-- **Secondary:** GitHub-documented course materials (public, auditable)
-- **Assessment:** Reflection-based written responses, structured assignments
-- **Evidence:** Public video corpus, interaction data, progression logs
+1. Resolve official entity and operating authority.
+2. Adopt governance, financial, faculty, safety and records policies with accountable people.
+3. Approve a bounded pilot and preserve actual participation, learner work, assessment, feedback and revisions.
+4. Document an improvement cycle and map evidence to current route-specific standards.
+5. Record each external application/review decision with its date, scope and source.
 
-### Seat Time Model (per course)
-
-20 videos × 10 minutes = 200 minutes instruction
-20 reflections × 5 minutes = 100 minutes engagement
-Total: 300 minutes (~5 hours) per course
-
-
-Per academic year (30 courses):
-
-30 courses × 5 hours = 150 instructional hours minimum
-Additional project/assessment time: ~50 hours
-Total estimated annual seat time: ~200 hours
-
-
-Equivalent to accreditor-accepted instructional block format.
-
-### Assessment Model
-- Comment-based reflection (timestamped, public)
-- Written response assignments (GitHub-tracked)
-- Portfolio documentation (per grade band)
-- Capstone projects (grades 9–12)
-- Standardized-equivalent assessments (grades 9–12, required for some states)
